[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n0_traveller"
text = "# DRAFT
# A traveller beside the porter on the carter's wagon, night 0: the road in from the white chapel to Aldgate at dusk.
# He opens as the carter pulls in and the cart with the covered body goes by (breaking off any talk on the road; traveller_road.tres is that talk). One choice, a short reply, and he's done.
== start
(The cart creaks by close enough to touch, its driver's hood pulled low. Something long lies under sacking on its bed.)
Traveller: You saw that, brother? A pilgrim, found in the ditch by the white chapel. The third this month.
Traveller: The carter says you're for the abbey inside Aldgate. The new porter, is it?
Traveller: Pilgrims go in at that gate to see the saint. Not all of them are seen to come out.
Traveller: And there's lights in it at night, moving about, when honest monks should be abed.
* What do people say it is? -> demon
* Who was the dead man? -> body
* (Say nothing, and pray for him.) -> pray

== demon
Traveller: A demon. A thing with horns, that walks the wall when the bells are done.
Traveller: I don't say it's true. I say I'd not sleep in there for the King's own purse.
-> end

== body
Traveller: Nobody knows. Nobody ever knows them. A badge on his hat, and his purse gone.
Traveller: Going to your saint, or coming from him. Nobody can say which.
-> end

== pray
(You say the words for the dead under your breath. The traveller watches you do it.)
Traveller: Say one for yourself while you're at it. You'll want it, where you're going.
-> end

== again
Traveller: Nearly at Aldgate. Keep your hood up, brother. The rain's coming on.
-> end

== leave
Traveller: Suit yourself. You'll see soon enough.
"
